```mdl
decision D-125: A plugin contributes a group as schema and data only, with no UI of its own: the form's existing fields render it.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.6]
```

```mdl
decision D-126: The project's name and description are edited in place, not behind an edit button.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-127: A group is a `ProjectCapabilities.ConfigGroup` (id, label, order, fields), and each field a key, a schema and a function from the project to a writable atom, with an optional `enabled` atom. The overview renders a group's fields as one nested form over a struct of their schemas and writes an edit through the field's atom; contributions with one id merge, and the project's own group is `agent`. This replaces the `ProjectSurface.Settings` surface. Fills in [D-124] and [D-125].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.5, F-5.6]
  why: A writable atom hides where a value lives, so an annotation on the project and state kept on one device are the same kind of field, and the form needs no knowledge of either.
  rejected:
    - A surface per group, which needs the contributor's own UI and lets only one plugin fill a group.
    - A capability declaring the group and surfaces filling it, which still needs the contributor's own UI.
    - Fields that name an annotation, which cannot hold a value kept on one device, such as a code folder.
```

```mdl
decision D-128: The status sits beside the name in a four-column row, and neither shows a label. react-ui-form's field override gains `appearance`: `title` renders a text field in react-ui's new `title` input variant, and `plain` drops the input's well, as the description does. The Specs list heads its own section, and its list keeps "Specs" as its accessible name. Fills in [D-126].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.1]
  why: The override says how one use of a field reads, which the schema cannot, and react-ui-form takes no classes of its own.
```

```mdl
decision D-129: The overview shows six artifacts, and Show all shows the rest in place until the companion exists. Fills in [D-123].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.3]
  why: Six fills two rows of the masonry at a plank's usual width.
```

```mdl
decision D-130: A folded group's summary counts each list, quotes each text and skips what is empty. Fills in [D-124].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.5]
  why: The counts are what tell a reader whether a group is worth opening.
```

```mdl
decision D-131: A milestone's progress counts the tasks of the level the overview shows, not every task in the project. Fills in [D-123].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.4]
  why: The overview already narrows to its level, and its Tasks tab lists the same tasks.
```

```mdl
decision D-132: The project's status is shown as a pill in the top right corner of the overview, using the form's pill presentation.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-133: The project's name and description line up with the headings of the overview's sections (Notes, Artifacts, Specs).
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-134: The status pill is required, so it offers no "None", and it sits at the end of the name's row. Supersedes the four-column row of [D-128]. Fills in [D-132].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.1]
  why: A project always has a status, and the name takes the rest of the row so a long name never pushes the pill.
```

```mdl
decision D-135: react-ui's Input and Textarea gain a `plain` variant with no well and no inline inset, and `title` drops the inset too; the form's `plain` and `title` appearances use them. Fills in [D-133].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.1]
  why: The inset was what pushed the text right of the headings, and react-ui-form takes no classes of its own.
  rejected:
    - Insetting the section headings to match, which would misalign them with every other form.
```

```mdl
decision D-136: Each project status has a colour, and its name is capitalized wherever the UI shows it.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-137: The gap between two of the overview's sections is wide enough that Artifacts, Milestones, Specs and Config never read as cramped together.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-138: The Specs add button sits on the Specs heading's row, so no gap opens between the heading and the specs, and the specs line up with the Config groups at the same level of nesting.
  date: 2026-11-03
