```mdl
decision D-139: The overview keeps one consistent edge down its left side and its right side.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-140: `Project`'s schema annotates its status with an option table, as `Task` does: Active in green, Paused in amber, Blocked in rose and Ended in neutral, each with an icon. The form's pill takes the title, icon and hue from it. Fills in [D-136].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.1]
  why: The form already reads option titles and hues from the schema, so every picker and pill of the status agrees with no code in the plugin.
  rejected:
    - Translations for the names, which the form's select does not read, and which would leave the colours in plugin code.
```

```mdl
decision D-141: A form section after another leaves three gaps above its heading, where rows inside a section leave one. A description edited in place is as tall as its text rather than three lines. Fills in [D-137].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.2]
  why: The rule lives on the section heading, so every form with sections gets the same rhythm without spacing of its own.
```

```mdl
decision D-142: react-ui-form's field override takes `appearance: 'section'` for an array, which renders the array as a section of its own with its label as the heading and its add button in the heading's actions. A form's array rows drop the list row's leading inset, so a row's fields start on the section's edge. Fills in [D-138] and [D-139].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.7]
  why: Wrapping the list in another section left the list's own header row, add button and all, under the section's heading.
  rejected:
    - The add button in a section's actions, written by the plugin, which would duplicate how the form creates an owned object.
```

```mdl
decision D-143: The overview's Notes section shows no description; once the notes have content it only takes up space.
  date: 2026-11-03
